The GitHub Action crashed with an `AttributeError: 'dict' object has no attribute 'split'` when `use_pyproject: true` was used and `[dependency-groups]` in `pyproject.toml` contained an `{include-group = "..."}` table. This happened because `find_black_version_in_array()` in `action/main.py` attempted to call `.split(";")` on every entry in the dependency array without verifying if the entry was a string.

I fixed this by adding a type check to skip non-string entries in `find_black_version_in_array()`. This ensures that only string-based dependency specifiers are processed, while dictionary-based include groups are safely ignored (as they are handled separately by the calling function `read_version_specifier_from_pyproject()`).

The fix was verified using a reproduction script that simulated the problematic `pyproject.toml` structure.

